    <string name="bind_failure">Failed to open camera due to an OS or hardware issue. Try rebooting.</string>
    <!-- Shown after a camera-extension mode (e.g. Night) is applied but its vendor implementation
         fails to bind: the mode is disabled and the camera falls back to a normal mode. Unlike
         bind_failure this is a handled, mode-specific recovery, not an OS/hardware failure, so it
         does not suggest rebooting. -->
    <string name="extension_mode_unavailable">This mode is unavailable on this device.</string>

    <!-- Shown when the camera can't record at the video quality the settings currently ask for,
         so that the settings screen doesn't keep claiming a quality that isn't actually in effect.
         %1$s is a quality such as "2160p (UHD)". A dropped quality is described as "a different
         quality" rather than a lower one because the fallback is Recorder's default order (1080p,
         then 720p, then 480p), which is higher than the requested quality if 480p was what got
         dropped. Stabilization outcomes are deliberately never surfaced (see onFeaturesSelected). -->
    <string name="quality_unsupported">%1$s isn\'t supported on this camera. Recording at a different quality.</string>
